en the SEV2 incident.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GSsguS8hM1wWe9UEEmxfSr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 release - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production release (error rate was 0.18 across us-east, us-west, and eu-west). Action taken: rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production, in all production regions. The rollback is verified in us-east, us-west, and eu-west. v2.3.1 was previously also flagged unhealthy in staging as v2.3.1-rc. Next steps: investigate the v2.3.1 failure before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2-2024", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back from v2.3.1 to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). The rollback is verified.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** It is the most recent release that was healthy in production. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc was unhealthy in staging.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It describes the failure, the rollback, and the next step of investigating v2.3.1 before any redeploy. It paged the on-call engineer.\n\nI did not re-check health or error rates after the rollback, so confirm that checkout-api is recovering.", "type": "text"}]}]}